WEBVTT

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.870
How long until we reach Heathrow?

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.000
We're on schedule. Scotland should be visible in two hours.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:32.840
Oh look, George, the ocean is beautiful!

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.930
Sheesh, even though your wife worked so hard to be here, you're just sleeping.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:44.770
Come on, I worked hard for this trip.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:50.020
Two days overtime in the area with the highest crime rate of New York.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.610
Ah, I knew you looked like a police officer.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:59.660
Excuse me, my name is Edmond Stark. Please to meet you.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.660
I couldn't help but overhear your conversation.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:06.290
It's no problem. I'm George Kimball.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.590
This is my wife, Alice.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:09.420
Pleased to meet you.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.630
I'm jealous, you get to travel with your wife.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.050
Pardon me.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:15.970
Well that's embarrassing...

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:27.520
How's the weather in London?

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:28.810
It seems to be cloudy.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:37.910
Some sun would be nice.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.320
It sure would.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:43.700
Enjoy the flight.

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:07.310
Isn't there another toilet?

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.070
Can you hold it?

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.030
I'm gonna blow.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.450
This way, then.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:33.880
What's wrong?

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:37.220
The lower deck toilets are clogged.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:39.880
May we use yours?

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:47.930
Go ahead, sir.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:10.210
Drop your gun.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.170
Hurry up.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.770
Terribly sorry, but I'm with them.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:04:01.260
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:12.600
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:24.360
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:30.660
The weak person I was is no more

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:36.250
I decided to just believe

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:43.380
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:47.220
I go towards you

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:54.940
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:59.070
I go towards you

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:03.110
Blown by the wind

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:08.570
Oh blown

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:19.960
Don't move!

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:22.590
We are hijacking this plane!

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.970
Raise your hands and put them behind your head.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:28.390
Now, bitch!

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.470
Hands behind your fucking head!

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:41.110
Jet Stream

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.960
Is there a VIP on board?

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.930
There are no VIPs on the list.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:10.220
I see.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:11.720
However...

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:12.930
However what?

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:14.770
There's a name bothering me.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.060
Duke Togo.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:21.190
Is there something you know about him?

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:25.150
He's a director of foreign trade, but there's no data on him.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.530
I've sent an inquiry to other agencies.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.700
Duke Togo, hm...

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.950
Lord Wilson, the radio.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:36.660
Eh?

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:44.630
We are not religious fanatics.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.630
We're simply greedy.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:51.970
Once we have landed at Heathrow, we will give you our next destination.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.640
Make preparations for our demands:

00:06:56.060 --> 00:07:00.650
First: One hundred million dollars in a Pelican case.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.020
Second: Five parachutes.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:07.280
Third: twenty kilograms of C4 and twenty detonators.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:10.320
Bring them to us peacefully.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:15.160
This is Raymond Barton of Scotland Yard.

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:18.330
I'll be your contact for negotiations.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:18.870
So-

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.920
We'll give you further instructions later.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.750
Could you release anyone?

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.510
We'll release the women and children.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:32.010
Be quick.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:35.470
We will arrive at Heathrow in an hour.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:44.560
A Pelican case is an American made, watertight case.

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:49.570
We can surmise they will attach a parachute and drop it over the ocean.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:56.200
If one of the parachutes is for the case, the other four must be for the hijackers.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.330
Then there must be four hijackers.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.080
Right.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:05.080
Do they plan on using the C4 to blow up the plane?

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:09.340
Or is there some other purpose for the explosives...

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:15.760
I will go to the Bank of England for the hundred million dollars.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:16.680
Yes sir.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.310
Take care of the rest in the remaining time.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:19.720
Yes sir.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:47.630
Hurry.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:30.460
It's been a while, Lord Wilson.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:36.380
This is the head of English Intelligence: Director Hume.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.800
I'm Barton, from Scotland Yard.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:47.310
We compared the passenger list with our records.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:53.070
The four hijackers are not professional criminals, and have no military records.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.690
There's also the C4...

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:59.820
it's almost certain they will kill someone with it.

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.370
What's going on here...

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:05.250
There's one more man I'm worried about.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:07.210
Who is it?

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:09.210
Duke Togo.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:12.130
He's simply a director of foreign trade.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.300
He has no criminal record.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:14.840
Is that right...

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:31.610
Golgo 13 is riding on that plane.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.150
He might be helpful in this situation.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:40.610
It's possible we will have no other choice.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:43.370
Golgo...

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:47.620
Hiring Golgo 13.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:25.330
This is good.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.370
We will release the women and children.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.880
Women and children have been released.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:41.630
One hundred and fifty seven remaining.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:43.720
I'm counting on you, Barton.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.600
Come this way and sit together!

00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:58.900
Hold on.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.570
Why are you so calm?

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.870
Answer me! I'm talking to you!

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:09.870
What's wrong?

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.710
There's something weird about this guy.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:16.630
Hm. He does seem to be being brave.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:28.890
Sit down!

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:36.480
It's about time for us to leave, Barton.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.400
How about you get out of harm's way?

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:39.690
Please wait!

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:44.320
I came on planning to stay until the end.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:48.240
If I stay, will you let the other passengers go?

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.870
Keeping everyone will not be easy.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.910
Quite the opposite, they will be a hindrance.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:59.040
He's probably right.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:03.010
Okay, we will only keep ten passengers.

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.050
One is this officer from Scotland Yard.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.510
who will be the remaining nine?

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:16.060
I will stay.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:19.270
I will also stay.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:23.490
It's also alright for me to stay.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:26.910
Mr. Stark, you are an old man. It would be better if you left.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:32.490
I am a doctor, it might be better if I stay.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.910
It's alright, Mr. Kimball.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.380
I too will stay.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:42.000
Me too.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.460
I'll stay on board.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.590
I'm in no hurry to return home.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.390
I will also stay.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:51.350
We need one more.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.140
What, won't anybody stand up?

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.980
U.. Umm...

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.360
This is hard for me to say...

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.200
You seem like a young, serious man.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:10.990
What do you say...

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:15.410
Won't you stay on board, to save the other passengers?

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:22.500
Alright.

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:26.380
Good. You'll also stay.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:35.270
At this rate, the hijackers will get away.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.890
Will England be able to face it?

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:41.940
Even with that, if the special forces shoot...

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:44.190
They will blow up the plane with the C4.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:48.400
As I thought, Golgo is our last chance.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.660
So we will have Golgo solve the problem?

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:52.660
That's right.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.450
But how will you contact him?

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.080
If the hijackers notice...

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:01.580
It could be dangerous for the passengers.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:07.050
We will have the hijackers deliver the message.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:12.180
Call Lord Wilson.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:18.640
The newspapers are piling up, and number thirteen is particularly good.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:25.610
One request to you: Keep your mother's life close to you.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:26.730
-Hume.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:28.860
Just what is this?!

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:33.370
Pass this message on to Bernard Kelly.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.240
But what are you saying here?

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:39.160
This is our last card.

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:42.880
If this fails, the passengers' lives are lost.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:45.880
Lord Wilson!

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:52.800
It's not everyone.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.550
The remaining number is not known.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.560
Barton's not out there either.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:05.860
The stairs are moving away!

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:07.730
Requesting permission to open fire!

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:13.530
The plane is taxiing out!

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:24.000
It's too soon to attack. Please standby.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:28.840
Why did you let that man remain on board?

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:32.550
Because I cannot stand him.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:37.050
Once we get off the ground, we will toss the money off the plane.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.680
Then we will follow suit.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.480
What happens next?

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:44.600
We will explose the plane.

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:48.820
And that man will still be here.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:50.860
There you go.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:54.360
Both this plane and his body will be buried at sea.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:55.570
Hey, listen!

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.320
There's a message coming in for you.

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:01.120
What's the message?

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:06.540
Well, I don't know, but it seems to be for you.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:18.890
The newspapers are piling up, and number 13 is particularly good.  One request for you, keep
your mother's life close to you.  -Hume.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:20.850
ARE YOU FUCKING WITH ME?

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:23.060
Saying incomprehensible things.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:25.690
Are you trying to mess with our heads?

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:27.310
Hold on Kerry.

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:31.690
However you look at it, it's ciphertext for someone here.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:32.990
A cipher?

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:33.360
Yeah.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:38.240
So if we read this, whomever's reaction is weird is...

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.200
We should look into this.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.120
Yeah.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:42.830
I have an idea.

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:57.510
I wonder if the message reached Golgo13 or not...

00:17:57.510 --> 00:18:02.100
The chance is small, but that cipher is the only chance for the message to reach Golgo.

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:06.310
All we can do now is pray and wait.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:21.240
Number thirteen!

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.380
No one reacted.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:33.590
What is that?

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:38.050
If you are hiding anything, we cannot guarantee the passengers lives!

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.010
Got that?

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:41.970
I understand.

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:45.520
It's just I don't understand what you are saying.

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:47.980
What's going on?

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:50.020
What's this, a memo?

00:18:50.650 --> 00:19:00.910
The newspapers are piling up, and number 13 is particularly good.  One request for you, keep
your mother's life close to you.  -Hume.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:02.280
Hume?

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:03.490
You know him?

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.410
Ah, I have a coworker with that name.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:12.710
As I thought. Barton.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:17.300
It's alright. After another hour they will all be blown up.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:24.810
What are you doing?

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:27.060
I have to use the toilet.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.180
Toilet eh? Fine.

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.360
Do it with the door open.

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:38.360
Hurry up and finish.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:49.410
Andre?

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.540
What's wrong Andre?

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.170
Don't move! I'll shoot you!

00:19:58.460 --> 00:19:59.760
Sit your ass down!

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:07.970
He.. He did it!

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:12.440
Hold on, I'm coming too.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:13.940
Don't move.

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:18.440
Don't help.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:19.320
But-

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:19.820
Don't.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.450
Listen to what he said.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:35.380
That's far enough.

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:43.180
You bastard..

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:14.960
Thanks to you, everyone remained calm.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:15.870
Thank you.

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.420
No, you are also to thank.

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:35.690
Excuse me a moment.

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:41.610
Mister Togo!

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:48.200
Thanks to your bravery, everyone was saved.

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:50.030
Thank you so much.

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:51.990
It was just a job.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:21:59.710
A job?

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.130
Is that so?

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:05.880
He said it was work.

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:12.390
What about Golgo's payment?

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:16.430
It's too high for SIS 43.

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:18.560
We'll let the English government cover the bill.

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:38.750
It doesn't matter anymore

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:44.300
Who craved freedom first

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:53.350
How we decided to part, and how we loved each other

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:55.520
As nostalgic and simply just that

00:22:55.560 --> 00:23:03.770
Once you've lost it you'll feel lonely

00:23:03.770 --> 00:23:07.440
You may have to overcome the pain

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:12.700
Many times with that cruel heart of yours

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:21.000
But you just can't become as strong as you've imagined

00:23:22.630 --> 00:23:25.590
It was just a dream

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:28.970
So let us return to tomorrow

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:33.970
In this calm night

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:36.140
There'll only be wanderers

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:41.310
But now you've awakened, so walk down that path of yours

00:23:41.390 --> 00:23:47.320
And even though time is fleeting

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:53.820
People sometimes desire too much

00:24:01.870 --> 00:24:05.960
A blood soaked female sniper is targeting Golgo.

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:10.380
While fascinated by a voluptuous body,

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:13.760
Golgo will recite a poem about the sound of falling rain for us.

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:21.020
When the Santa Ana winds blow, the battle between the two snipers will begin.

00:24:20.230 --> 00:24:25.020
Santa Ana

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:23.230
Next time, on Gordon Freeman:

00:24:23.230 --> 00:24:24.440
Santa Ana

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:28.650
Don't stand behind him if you value your life.
